course: dictionary
lesson: 16086
title: Washable
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Washable is an adjective, a word that describes a thing. It tells you that something can be washed without being damaged. «The paint on my shirt is washable.» The word is made from wash and -able, which means can be, so washable means can be washed.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Mum said the markers are washable, so the stains will come out in the bath.» The stains come out with water, so washable must mean it can be washed clean. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the markers can be washed clean" makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Labels on clothes often say «machine washable», which means the item can go in a washing machine. Washable is also used for paint, crayons and markers. Look for it on packets and labels when you shop.
fact: Washable means it can be washed without being damaged.
fact: The word washable is made from wash and -able, which means can be.
fact: «Washable paint» comes out of clothes and off walls with water.
fact: «Machine washable» means the item can go in a washing machine.
exercise: «The label says this jumper is machine washable.» What does machine washable mean? | It is made of metal | It must never be wet | *It can go in a washing machine without being damaged | It is very soft and warm
exercise: Mia used washable markers for her poster. Why was Mum glad about that? | The poster would never come off the paper | *Mum could wash the marks off Mia's hands and the table with water | The markers were made of wood | The markers were very dry
exercise: «The washable paint came off the table easily.» Find and copy one word that means can be washed without being damaged. | paint | table | *washable | easily
test: «Dad bought washable crayons so the walls would stay clean.» What does washable mean here? | Can be broken into pieces | Can be eaten | *Can be cleaned off with water | Can be painted over with glue
test: Which label shows that a T-shirt can go in the washing machine? | *Machine washable | Hand wash only | Do not wash | Dry clean only
exam: Ella says, «The stain on my bag is washable.» What does she mean? | It is made of water | It can never be cleaned | *It can be washed clean without being damaged | It is a very dirty bag
